Z||000001||mrossum||06-02-2001||09:48 AM||||cracked head lets combustion gas into the cooling system. then when engine is shut off, the pressure in the cooling system forces water into the oil.......||||reg||1
Z||000002||84Bill||06-02-2001||11:59 AM||||Coolant under pressure will not boil BUT if the crack in the head pumps air into the system viola! Not to mention it overpressurizes the system and forces coolant out the vent pipe. <p>[This message has been edited by 84Bill (edited 06-02-2001).]||||reg||14
